Insertion Sort works like how you sort playing cards in your hand:
✔ Take one card (element)
✔ Compare it with left side (sorted part)
✔ Insert it at correct position
✔ Shift elements as needed
That’s why it's called INSERTION sort.


📌 Concept in One Line
👉 Take one element, move left until you find its correct position.
Time complexity


Best Case (O(n)):
This occurs when the array is already sorted.
Only one comparison is needed for each element
to verify it is in the correct position.

Average Case (O(n²)) and Worst Case (O(n²))

O(1): Insertion Sort is an in-place sorting algorithm

Insertion Sort is a stable sorting algorithm
